<title>INDIA: INDIA'S RBI SEEN 280 BLN RUPEES CAPEX BY COMPANIES.</title>
<headline>INDIA'S RBI SEEN 280 BLN RUPEES CAPEX BY COMPANIES.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it expected Indian firms to incur 280 billion rupees in capital expenditure during 1997/98 (April-March).</p>
<p>&quot;The total capital expenditure to be incurred in 1997/98 for which sanctions were accorded upto 1996/97 amounted to 447.75 billion rupees,&quot; the RBI Bulletin for August said.</p>
<p>&quot;With 1997/98 expected to be another normal monsoon year, the general perception is that the economy is expected to grow at around the same level as in the previous year.&quot;</p>
</text>
